.TH FILE-CONVERT 1 "2026-09-04" "file-convert 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
file\-convert \- convert image and document files to another format
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B file\-convert
.I format
.IR file ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B file\-convert
converts each
.I file
to
.IR format ,
writing the result next to the original. It is the command behind the
"Convert" entries that
.B context\-menu\-converter
adds to Linux file managers, and works equally well on its own.
.PP
The engine is chosen from what each source file actually is, not from its
name: images go through ImageMagick, everything else through LibreOffice. A
single command may therefore mix both kinds and each file still takes the
right path.
.PP
The original file is always kept, and an existing file is never overwritten:
if
.I photo.png
already exists, the output becomes
.IR photo\-1.png ,
then
.IR photo\-2.png ,
and so on.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I format
Target format: \fBpng\fR, \fBjpg\fR, \fBwebp\fR, \fBavif\fR, or any other
format ImageMagick can write. AVIF and HEIC require the matching ImageMagick
delegates, which some distributions ship separately.
.TP
.I file
One or more files. Arguments that are not regular files are reported as
failures and skipped.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENCODING
.TP
.B jpg
Transparency is flattened onto white, since JPEG has no alpha channel; quality 92.
.TP
.B webp
Quality 90.
.TP
.B avif
Quality 60.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every file was converted.
.TP
.B 1
At least one file failed, or the arguments were invalid.
.SH PROGRESS
A conversion that takes more than a moment reports progress: a bar on the
terminal, or a desktop notification that updates in place.
.PP
For images the percentage is real, read from ImageMagick's progress monitor.
LibreOffice reports nothing while it works, so a single document gets an
indeterminate bar; with several files the bar tracks how many are done.
.PP
Notification daemons that support the
.B value
hint, such as Plasma's, draw a real progress bar. GNOME Shell's does not, so
the bar is drawn as text in the notification body.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
When run from a terminal, results are printed to standard output. When run from
a file manager, a desktop notification reports how many files succeeded and
names those that failed, using
.BR notify\-send (1);
fatal errors use
.BR zenity (1)
or
.BR kdialog (1)
if available.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Convert one file:
.PP
.RS
.EX
file\-convert png photo.webp
.EE
.RE
.PP
Convert every PNG in the current directory to JPG:
.PP
.RS
.EX
file\-convert jpg *.png
.EE
.RE
.PP
Convert a document to PDF:
.PP
.RS
.EX
file\-convert pdf rapport.docx
.EE
.RE
.SH REQUIREMENTS
For images,
.BR magick (1)
(ImageMagick 7) or
.BR convert (1)
(ImageMagick 6). For documents,
.BR soffice (1)
(LibreOffice). Only the engine a given selection needs has to be present.
.PP
Document conversion runs LibreOffice against a throwaway user profile, so it
works while LibreOffice is open and never disturbs the running instance.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR magick (1),
.BR soffice (1),
.BR notify\-send (1)
.SH BUGS
Report issues at
.UR https://github.com/TheoG71/context\-menu\-converter/issues
.UE .
